    [Feature][Ops] Gather RoPE cos/sin rows from the contiguous flat base (#19247)
    
    ## Why
    
    Every MTP draft step calls `get_cos_and_sin_mla(positions)` to gather
    RoPE cos/sin rows. On NPU, indexing the **strided per-half views**
    (`_cos_cache[positions]`, `_sin_cache[positions]`) makes `aclnnIndex`
    materialize the **entire cache table** on every lookup, while the
    effective payload is only `bs * rotary_dim * 2` bytes:
    
    - 1M-row BF16 cache => ~134 MB written / ~250 MB read per lookup, ~420
    us each;
    - with MTP K=5 that is **12 full-cache materializations per decode
    step** (2 lookups x 6 forwards), ~4.2 ms/step (~5.7% of the step period)
    on GLM-5.2 DP16 x TP2.
    
    (GPU keeps lazy views; the NPU aclnn path does not, so the row gather
    degenerates into a full-table copy.)
    
    ## What
    
    Register a contiguous **flat view of the interleaved base table** at
    registration time (`_cos_sin_flat`, where `_cos_cache[i] == flat[2i]`
    and `_sin_cache[i] == flat[2i+1]`) and gather rows from it
    (`flat[positions*2]` / `flat[positions*2+1]`). The flat base is
    contiguous, so the same row gather is a plain copy (~10 us):
    
    - the fast path is **unconditional** — no config switch. The fix is
    zero-risk (bitwise identical) and benefits every model on the
    interleaved-registration path (DeepSeek-V3.2 family, GLM, Kimi, ...);
    - the legacy strided gather remains as the fallback for registrations
    that do not provide the flat view (the non-interleaved
    `_record_cos_and_sin_cache` path resets it to `None`);
    - the flat view shares storage with the registered derived buffers, so
    the sleep-mode wake restore that rebuilds them in place covers it as
    well.
    
    ## Correctness
    
    **Bitwise identical** to the legacy path: same physical storage, same
    rows, integer-only index arithmetic (`positions * 2` / `+ 1` on int
    indices), pure byte copy, identical out-of-bounds domain (`2p < 2N ⟺ p <
    N`). Proven by unit tests (`tests/ut/ops/test_rotary_flat_gather.py`):
    flat-vs-fallback bitwise equality (duplicates / empty / boundary
    positions / `use_cache` path), plus registration semantics (storage
    sharing with the derived buffers, first-wins, non-interleaved override
    resets the flat view).
    
    ## Performance
    
    Measured on GLM-5.2 (2x Atlas A3, 32 dies, DP16 x TP2, EP32, MTP K=5):
    removes **12 full-cache materializations per decode step (~4.2
    ms/step)**; each lookup becomes ~10 us regardless of cache size,
    reversing the size sensitivity of the legacy path (whose cost was
    proportional to the full 1M-row table, independent of batch/context).
    
    ## Testing
    
    - [x] `py_compile` + structural assertions for touched files
    - [x] New UT: `tests/ut/ops/test_rotary_flat_gather.py`
    - [x] NPU server validation (trace assertion:
    `aclnnIndex_SliceAiCore_Slice` on the rope lookup path 12/step -> 0;
    draft token sequence bit-identical vs legacy path)
    
    Measured on GLM-5.2 (2 x A3, 32 dies, PD disaggregation, DP2 x TP16,
    EP32, MTP K=5):
    
    **The ITL is optimized by ~3.5ms**
    
    **NOTE:** This is the first of two PRs splitting #18219 (the two
    features are file-orthogonal and independently revertable). The sibling
    PR (multistream MTP metadata overlap) will be submitted separately;
    #18219 can be closed once both land.
    
